.TH CHTTPSVR_ENGINE_WAIT 3 "2026-07-10" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Functions"
.SH NAME
chttpsvr_engine_wait \- wait for the engine thread to exit
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <chttpserver.h>

void chttpsvr_engine_wait(void);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
Blocks the calling thread until the shared facil.io engine has fully
stopped; whether a stop was already triggered before this call, is
triggered concurrently, or is not triggered until sometime after this
call (this blocks indefinitely if nothing ever stops the engine, e.g.
an external SIGTERM handler calling chttpsvr_engine_stop() at some
later, unknown time).

The engine is shared with chttpclient's async engine
(chttpclient_do_async/_streaming); dropping the last reference from
either module (e.g. destroying the last chttpsvr via
__chttpsvr_destroy, or the last chttpclient async request completing)
triggers an asynchronous teardown that does not itself block the
caller that triggered it; this function is the explicit escape
hatch for programs that need to synchronise with that shutdown, or
with an externally signalled chttpsvr_engine_stop() call.

Safe to call concurrently from multiple threads; each blocks until
the engine is confirmed fully stopped, regardless of which caller's
release or chttpsvr_engine_stop() call was the one that triggered it.

After this function returns, the engine logger is cleared so that any
remaining facil.io atexit callbacks do not access a freed clog handle.

Safe to call before the engine has ever started (no-op).
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR chttpsvr_engine_stop (3),
.BR chttpsvr_start (3),
.BR __chttpsvr_destroy (3),
.BR chttpsvr_set_engine_logger (3)
